+
+## Current native parameter extension (October 24, 2026)
+
+The separate `workspace/parametric/` family now exposes `mode=all|largest_owned`.
+The default returns the exact canonical program bytes; production generator
+source and its reviewed geometry contract remain unchanged. The alternate
+assigns zeros to the smallest enclosing operative frame, counts the disjoint
+ownership regions, and fills only every region tied for the largest positive
+count. It preserves colored outlines and losing/exterior zeros.
+
+The extension supports 2..6 demos and 1..4 queries independently, ordinarily
+three demos and four novel queries. Two constructive demonstrations (outer/middle
+tie, then an innermost sole winner) identify the setting among twelve declared
+executable hypotheses. Input streams match across modes and preserve prefixes
+when counts change. Extended scenes use two or three outlines at 7..30 cells per
+dimension, including lawful nonoperative terminals and full-canvas 30x30 stress.
+The first tie example also rejects painting inside selected frames without
+respecting their true ownership masks. A weak one-demo lesson permitting the
+single-tie-winner shortcut is retained with its repairing tie example.
+
+Focused verification: 27 tests passed; the final self-review executed 68 protected
+Racket evaluations over twelve programs, four three-demo/four-query episodes,
+and a separate 36/36 Python API request sweep. Eight public files passed the
+existing export checker; injected answer leakage, Boolean cells and duplicate
+queries were rejected. Native qualification passed both settings at seeds 0 and
+17. Exact receipts are in `checks/94d475bf67ba/` in this return; the source-bound
+task inventory is `workspace/parametric/evidence/manifest.json`.
+
+The causal witness changes only the intermediate counts from true disjoint
+ownership to raw contained zeros. The qualified alternate and counterfactual
+therefore choose different frames while keeping the same true ownership write
+mask. The native witness helper replays both final labels through protected
+Racket. Intermediate descriptions remain authored metadata.
+
+Current status is reviewer-ready with native qualification, pending owner
+integration and exact-source acceptance. No training admission is asserted.
+Finite rivals do not establish universal uniqueness. Largest enclosed-zero-
+component selection is an equivalent implementation on this strict grammar.
+Broken/touching/disconnected borders and other distractors remain outside it.
+`audit.py` is the reusable reproduction and compact example-export tool; its
+README gives commands, scope, and single-query public projection behavior.
 
